LAB Overview

Active Directory: + Windows Networking
This lab demonstrates the setup and management of an Active Directory environment in a virtualized Windows network. It includes installing and configuring a Domain Controller with DHCP, DNS, and Organizational Units,
creating users with PowerShell automation scripts, and joining a client VM to the domain. The lab also covers internal networking, NAT routing, and troubleshooting connectivity issues, showing practical problem solving 
and system administration skills. Completing this lab reinforces my practical skills in managing Active Directory, configuring clients, and troubleshooting network connectivity
